of <strong>47\u00b0F</strong> was the 13th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 88 since 1939, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 58\u00b0F, and the record is 82\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Paducah's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Paducah has set <strong>70 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 112 that chance alone would give, and <strong>120 record highs</strong>, close to the 111 that chance alone would give. The 1940s hold the most record highs of any decade (60). Paducah's all-time high is 108\u00b0F, on July 17, 1942.","t_chg":"Paducah has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 84 complete years: Paducah's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.21\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.31), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1938. Paducah's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.33), about +1.6\u00b0F since 1938.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Paducah has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Paducah's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.09 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +1.95), about +9.5 inches since 1938. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 50.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (74.85 in); the driest, 1963 (28.20 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}